# component: combobox
# decisions: A11Y-16, A11Y-2, A11Y-3, A11Y-4, A11Y-9, API-19, API-26, API-27, BRD-1, DOC-1, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-3, FOC-5, FOC-6, FRM-4, INT-1, OVL-13
# hunks:
#   API-19: `ComboboxItem` calls Item's `useItemDescriptionId()`, provides its `register` through
#     `ItemDescriptionContext`, and sets `aria-describedby` on the option once an `ItemDescription`
#     inside it registers, so a two-line option (`ItemContent` > `ItemTitle` + `ItemDescription`)
#     reads its second line as the option's accessible description. A one-line option links nothing.
#   FOC-1, FOC-3, FOC-6: `ComboboxChips` loses `focus-within:ring-3 focus-within:ring-ring/50` and
#     keeps a `focus-within:border-ring/70` tint; `ComboboxChipsInput`'s `outline-none` becomes
#     `outline-hidden`, so the FOC-7 forced-colours block has an outline to repaint. The
#     single-line field's own focus chrome comes from `InputGroup`.
#   FOC-5: the chips field's invalid tint becomes
#     `not-focus-within:has-aria-invalid:border-destructive` (and its dark counterpart), so focus
#     outranks it; the `has-aria-invalid` halo rings go with the rest.
#   INT-1: `cursor-default` is removed from `ComboboxItem`, so a row shows the hand cursor the one
#     global rule gives every `[role="option"]`.
#   FRM-4: `data-disabled:pointer-events-none` on `ComboboxItem` and `has-disabled:pointer-events-none`
#     on `ComboboxChip` are dropped, so a disabled row or chip stays hoverable and a Tooltip can
#     explain it.
#   A11Y-3, A11Y-4: `ComboboxEmpty` no longer hides itself with `hidden` (`display: none`). It IS
#     Base UI's own polite live region, and Base UI documents that hiding it that way breaks the
#     announcement, so it stays in layout at `h-0 overflow-hidden` and expands when the list empties.
#   A11Y-16: the toggle inside `ComboboxInput`, the chip's remove control and the field's clear
#     control get an `aria-label`. Upstream renders all three as icon-only `<button>`s holding an
#     `XIcon` or a `ChevronDownIcon` and no text, and Base UI supplies no name for any of them —
#     the chip's own label is a SIBLING of its button rather than its content, so they read as
#     "button" to a screen reader. Batch 3 recorded this hunk under A11Y-5 and FLAGGED it for MK,
#     because A11Y-5's letter is the `sr-only ", "` separator between sibling name parts and does
#     not authorise naming a control. MK settled it on 2026-09-18 by adding A11Y-16 — every
#     interactive control carries an accessible name — which is the row cited here. The hunk never
#     changed; only its citation did.
#   A11Y-9: the toggle inside `ComboboxInput` takes `tabIndex={-1}`. While the popup is open Base
#     UI marks the WHOLE trailing addon `aria-hidden="true"` — the addon sits outside the popup,
#     and the input beside it is the anchor the engine keeps exposed — so the toggle was a tab stop
#     inside an `aria-hidden` subtree, which no screen reader will name (axe: SERIOUS
#     `aria-hidden-focus`). A11Y-9 is that invariant, stated for the modal surfaces; Batch 5
#     applied it to the non-modal toast on the same reading, and this is the third surface. Base
#     UI's own `Combobox.Clear` — the addon's other control — already ships `tabIndex={-1}`, and
#     APG's editable combobox keeps its popup toggle out of the tab sequence because the
#     `role="combobox"` input beside it already opens the list, so the attribute costs no keyboard
#     affordance. The addon is deliberately NOT made `inert`: that would kill the mouse too, and
#     clicking the chevron to close an open popup has to keep working. It is set at the ONE call
#     site that puts a button inside the region Base UI hides, so the standalone `ComboboxTrigger`
#     of the Popup composition keeps its own tab stop. `combobox.test.tsx` now audits the open
#     state with NO axe suppression list, and pins the engine's shape beside it, so the hunk fails
#     as stale the day Base UI stops hiding the addon. Before this, the violation was RECORDED by
#     an `aria-hidden-focus` exemption in the test and published as known behaviour on the docs
#     page; both are gone. Worth reporting to Base UI.
#   A11Y-2: `ComboboxChipsInput` gains `min-h-6`. Upstream's chips input measures 20px tall inside
#     the 32px chips field, which is under the 24px target floor; the input is transparent, so the
#     extra 4px changes nothing visible.
#   OVL-13: `ComboboxContent` reads `useInternalThemeScope()` and attaches it to the Positioner
#     inside the Portal; `tooling/verify-portal-theme-scope.mjs` inventories this host.
#   BRD-1: `ComboboxContent` draws a real 1px `border border-border` instead of upstream's
#     `ring-1 ring-foreground/10` box-shadow outline (MK reversed BRD-1 to ours, 23-09-2026). A
#     border survives forced colours and matches `foundations/elevation`; nothing else moves.
#   API-26: Base UI's `Combobox.Input` reads the `Field` context itself (label, description and
#     error ids, `aria-invalid`); `combobox.test.tsx` pins it. One hunk: inside a `Field`, Base UI
#     also hands the Field label's id to `Combobox.Trigger` as `aria-labelledby`, which outranks
#     the addon toggle's own `aria-label`, so a second element answered to the field's name. The
#     `ComboboxInput` addon toggle passes `aria-labelledby={undefined}` and keeps "Show
#     suggestions"; the input is the one control the Field names.
#   API-27: a new `ComboboxStatus` part re-exports Base UI's `Combobox.Status` — the engine's own
#     polite `role="status"` region for an asynchronously loaded list (DS-40, approved by MK
#     24-09-2026). It carries `data-slot="combobox-status"` and is `sr-only` unless `visible`, which
#     sets `data-visible` and shows it as a muted row that collapses its padding while empty. It is
#     never hidden with `display: none`, `hidden` or `aria-hidden` — Base UI documents that the root
#     must stay mounted — so a consumer renders it as a sibling of `ComboboxList` and toggles its
#     children.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
